{
  "rationale": "Use a minimal two-plant DES: one plant for sensor outcomes and one for motion capabilities. Encode the exploration policy in small deterministic specifications that separate safe forward progress from obstacle-triggered recovery. The policy strongly prefers move_forward in clear conditions, uses directed one-shot turns for side/front obstacles, allows a rare one-shot backward escape only after front blockage, and reserves full_rotate for a dedicated repeated-failure helper path.",
  "strategy": [
    "Split sensing and actuation into separate plant automata so specifications can bind uncontrollable obstacle observations to exactly one safe controllable action.",
    "Use perception/decision states plus one-shot commit/recovery states so uncontrollable events are total in every state, obstacle events preempt when safety-critical, and forward exploration resumes quickly after recovery."
  ],
